<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia July building approvals up 8.1 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia July building approvals up 8.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian dwelling unit building approvals rose a seasonally-adjusted 8.1 percent in July to 10,619 from 9,824 in June, compared with 11,280 in July 1995, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Economists' median forecasts had been for building approvals to rise 4.0 percent in July.  </p>
<p>Australian housing building approvals-</p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJUSTED		  July 96  June 96  July 95</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  7,050   6,905    7,503</p>
<p>    Total houses			     7,161   6,930    7,652</p>
<p>    Total private dwelling units	 9,986   9,700   10,744</p>
<p>    Total dwelling units		  10,619   9,824   11,280</p>
<p>    Value residential building (A$ bln) 1.26    1.15     1.38</p>
<p>    Value total buildings (A$ bln)	2.17    2.03     2.09</p>
<p>TREND ESTIMATES</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  6,992   7,011    7,526</p>
<p>    Total Dwelling Units		  10,375  10,354   11,161</p>
<p>The Bureau said the seasonaly adjusted number of private sector houses approved in July rose by 2.1 percent while the number of other residential dwelling units approved rose by 19.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
